  "lines": [
    {
      "text": "This Irish ring says whether you're single.",
      "scene": {
        "kind": "hook",
        "show": "claddagh",
        "metal": "yellow",
        "color": "#4cc3a8"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "It's the Claddagh ring, named for a fishing village by Galway.",
      "scene": {
        "kind": "title",
        "text": "Claddagh",
        "sub": "A fishing village by Galway",
        "color": "#f7c23a"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "The design is two hands holding a crowned heart.",
      "scene": {
        "kind": "jewel",
        "piece": "claddagh",
        "metal": "yellow",
        "label": "Two hands, one crowned heart",
        "velvet": "#ec6a9c",
        "color": "#5bb4e8"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "The hands are said to stand for friendship,",
      "scene": {
        "kind": "title",
        "text": "Friendship",
        "sub": "The hands",
        "color": "#c8dc3c"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "the heart for love and the crown for loyalty.",
      "scene": {
        "kind": "title",
        "text": "Love and loyalty",
        "sub": "The heart and the crown",
        "color": "#ec6a9c"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Legend says a Galway goldsmith, Richard Joyce, made the first one.",
      "scene": {
        "kind": "cast",
        "setting": "workshop",
        "name": "Richard Joyce",
        "role": "Galway goldsmith",
        "color": "#a98be0",
        "cast": [
          {
            "outfit": "apron",
            "outfitColor": "#5bb4e8",
            "hair": "long",
            "hairColor": "#6a4a30",
            "skin": "#efc9a6",
            "expression": "focused",
            "facial": "beard",
            "prop": "gem",
            "propTone": "#f7c23a"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "In the tale, Algerian pirates sold him to a goldsmith.",
      "scene": {
        "kind": "journey",
        "icon": "ship",
        "label": "Captured at sea",
        "color": "#5bb4e8",
        "from": {
          "name": "Galway",
          "x": 0.15,
          "y": 0.2
        },
        "to": {
          "name": "Algiers",
          "x": 0.8,
          "y": 0.8
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "King William the Third later ordered his release,",
      "scene": {
        "kind": "cast",
        "setting": "palace",
        "name": "King William the Third",
        "role": "Ordered his release",
        "color": "#f0552e",
        "cast": [
          {
            "outfit": "royal",
            "outfitColor": "#c8314a",
            "hair": "curly",
            "hairColor": "#6a4a30",
            "skin": "#f3d6bd",
            "expression": "proud",
            "hat": "crown",
            "facial": "mustache"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "and back in Galway, he gave the ring to his sweetheart.",
      "scene": {
        "kind": "cast",
        "setting": "street",
        "color": "#c8dc3c",
        "cast": [
          {
            "outfit": "coat",
            "outfitColor": "#3a2a22",
            "hair": "long",
            "hairColor": "#6a4a30",
            "skin": "#efc9a6",
            "expression": "smile",
            "facial": "beard"
          },
          {
            "outfit": "dress",
            "outfitColor": "#ec6a9c",
            "hair": "updo",
            "hairColor": "#3a2a1e",
            "skin": "#f3d6bd",
            "expression": "smile"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "The oldest ring, from about 1700, is in a Galway museum.",
      "say": "The oldest ring, from about seventeen hundred, is in a Galway museum.",
      "scene": {
        "kind": "jewel",
        "piece": "claddagh",
        "metal": "yellow",
        "label": "About 1700",
        "velvet": "#f7c23a",
        "color": "#4cc3a8"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "By tradition, heart out on the right hand means single.",
      "scene": {
        "kind": "jewel",
        "piece": "claddagh",
        "metal": "yellow",
        "label": "Right hand, heart out",
        "velvet": "#a98be0",
        "color": "#ec6a9c"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Heart in means taken, and on the left hand it means married.",
      "scene": {
        "kind": "cast",
        "setting": "plain",
        "color": "#5bb4e8",
        "cast": [
          {
            "outfit": "casual",
